  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 233 AM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nShowers and thunderstorms were ongoing early this morning across \nnorthwest Kansas where mid-level waa was present. A stray shower or \nstorm may brush parts of central Kansas through the early morning \nhours but the more meaningful precipitation is expected to \nremain north and west of the area. The persistent sfc trough \naxis bisecting western Kansas may move slightly closer towards \nour forecast area on Tuesday as the mid/upper ridge translates \neastward but the focus for any isolated storm activity is still \nexpected to remain north and west of the area. As we move into \nWed-Thu, rising heights are progged as the mid/upper ridge \nbegins to build back over the area leading to a continuation of \nhot and dry weather for the area. Temperatures may begin to \ntrend up once again over the weekend as the ridge amplifies \nacross the central CONUS leading to a continuation of hot, \nbreezy and dry weather conditions through the period.",
